          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef compute_first_order_ale(predict_fn, X: np.ndarray, col_idx: int, n_bins: int = 10) -> tuple[float, float, float]:\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n    xj = X[:, col_idx]\n    edges = np.quantile(xj, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1))\n    edges[0] -= 1e-6\n    edges[-1] += 1e-6\n    mids = 0.5 * (edges[:-1] + edges[1:])\n    bids = np.clip(np.digitize(xj, edges) - 1, 0, n_bins - 1)\n    diffs = np.zeros(n_bins, dtype=float)\n    counts = np.zeros(n_bins, dtype=float)\n    for k in range(n_bins):\n        mask = bids == k\n        counts[k] = np.sum(mask)\n        X_hi = X[mask].copy()\n        X_lo = X[mask].copy()\n        X_hi[:, col_idx] = edges[k + 1]\n        X_lo[:, col_idx] = edges[k]\n        diffs[k] = float(np.mean(predict_fn(X_hi) - predict_fn(X_lo)))\n    ale_mid = np.r_[0.0, np.cumsum(diffs)[:-1]] + 0.5 * diffs\n    ale_centered = ale_mid - float(np.sum(ale_mid * counts) / np.sum(counts))\n    slope = float(np.polyfit(mids, ale_centered, 1)[0])\n    return (round(slope, 4), round(float(ale_centered[0]), 4), round(float(ale_centered[-1]), 4))\n```"
