          "code": "import math\nfrom itertools import combinations\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\nn, d = 600, 5\nX = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(n, d))\ny = 2.5 * X[:, 0] - 1.8 * X[:, 1] + 2.2 * (X[:, 0] > 0.0) * X[:, 2] + 0.9 * X[:, 3] + rng.normal(0.0, 0.25, size=n)\n\nrf = RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=12, max_depth=4, min_samples_leaf=8, random_state=42)\nrf.fit(X, y)\n\n\ndef extend_path(m_path, p_zero, p_one, feat_idx):\n    \"\"\"Subrutin EXTEND TreeSHAP (Lundberg et al. 2018/2020) berdurasi polinomial.\"\"\"\n    L = len(m_path)\n    out = [row.copy() for row in m_path]\n    out.append([feat_idx, p_zero, p_one, 1.0 if L == 0 else 0.0])\n    for i in range(L - 1, -1, -1):\n        out[i + 1][3] += p_one * out[i][3] * (i + 1) / (L + 1)\n        out[i][3] = p_zero * out[i][3] * (L - i) / (L + 1)\n    return out\n\n\ndef unwind_path(m_path, idx):\n    \"\"\"Subrutin UNWIND untuk menghapus kontribusi duplikat fitur pada jalur pohon.\"\"\"\n    L = len(m_path) - 1\n    pz, po = m_path[idx][1], m_path[idx][2]\n    n_val = m_path[L][3]\n    out = [row.copy() for row in m_path[:L]]\n    for i in range(L - 1, -1, -1):\n        if po != 0.0:\n            t = out[i][3]\n            out[i][3] = n_val * (L + 1) / ((i + 1) * po)\n            n_val = t - out[i][3] * pz * (L - i) / (L + 1)\n        else:\n            out[i][3] = (out[i][3] * (L + 1)) / (pz * (L - i))\n    for i in range(idx, L):\n        out[i][0] = m_path[i + 1][0]\n        out[i][1] = m_path[i + 1][1]\n        out[i][2] = m_path[i + 1][2]\n    return out\n\n\ndef treeshap_single_tree(tree, x_row: np.ndarray, n_features: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Exact Path-Dependent TreeSHAP O(L * D^2) langsung di atas sklearn.tree.Tree.\"\"\"\n    phi = np.zeros(n_features, dtype=float)\n    feat = tree.feature\n    thresh = tree.threshold\n    left = tree.children_left\n    right = tree.children_right\n    vals = tree.value[:, 0, 0]\n    covers = tree.weighted_n_node_samples\n\n    def recurse(node, m_path, p_z, p_o, p_i):\n        m_cur = extend_path(m_path, p_z, p_o, p_i)\n        if left[node] == -1:\n            for i in range(1, len(m_cur)):\n                unw = unwind_path(m_cur, i)\n                w_sum = sum(r[3] for r in unw)\n                phi[int(m_cur[i][0])] += w_sum * (m_cur[i][2] - m_cur[i][1]) * vals[node]\n            return\n        d_j = int(feat[node])\n        hot = left[node] if x_row[d_j] <= thresh[node] else right[node]\n        cold = right[node] if hot == left[node] else left[node]\n        iz, io = 1.0, 1.0\n        k_match = next((k for k in range(1, len(m_cur)) if int(m_cur[k][0]) == d_j), -1)\n        if k_match != -1:\n            iz, io = m_cur[k_match][1], m_cur[k_match][2]\n            m_cur = unwind_path(m_cur, k_match)\n        recurse(hot, m_cur, iz * covers[hot] / covers[node], io, d_j)\n        recurse(cold, m_cur, iz * covers[cold] / covers[node], 0.0, d_j)\n\n    recurse(0, [], 1.0, 1.0, -1)\n    return phi\n\n\ndef brute_force_path_tree_shap(tree, x_row: np.ndarray, n_features: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Verifikasi eksak O(2^d) menggunakan ekspektasi jalur pohon bersyarat.\"\"\"\n    feat, thresh = tree.feature, tree.threshold\n    left, right = tree.children_left, tree.children_right\n    vals, covers = tree.value[:, 0, 0], tree.weighted_n_node_samples\n\n    def exp_val(node, S_set):\n        if left[node] == -1:\n            return float(vals[node])\n        d_j = int(feat[node])\n        if d_j in S_set:\n            nxt = left[node] if x_row[d_j] <= thresh[node] else right[node]\n            return exp_val(nxt, S_set)\n        wl = covers[left[node]] / covers[node]\n        return wl * exp_val(left[node], S_set) + (1.0 - wl) * exp_val(right[node], S_set)\n\n    vc = {}\n    for r in range(n_features + 1):\n        for S in combinations(range(n_features), r):\n            vc[S] = exp_val(0, set(S))\n    phi = np.zeros(n_features)\n    for j in range(n_features):\n        others = [k for k in range(n_features) if k != j]\n        for r in range(n_features):\n            w = math.factorial(r) * math.factorial(n_features - r - 1) / math.factorial(n_features)\n            for S in combinations(others, r):\n                phi[j] += w * (vc[tuple(sorted(S + (j,)))] - vc[S])\n    return phi\n\n\nx_test = np.array([1.1, -0.7, 1.4, 0.6, 1.9])\nphi_treeshap = np.mean([treeshap_single_tree(est.tree_, x_test, d) for est in rf.estimators_], axis=0)\nphi_bruteforce = np.mean([brute_force_path_tree_shap(est.tree_, x_test, d) for est in rf.estimators_], axis=0)\nbase_val = float(np.mean([est.tree_.value[0, 0, 0] for est in rf.estimators_]))\npred_rf = float(rf.predict(x_test.reshape(1, -1))[0])\n\nprint(f\"RandomForest (T=12, D=4, d=5) | Base={base_val:.4f} | Pred={pred_rf:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"TreeSHAP Polinomial O(TLD^2) : {np.round(phi_treeshap, 5).tolist()}\")\nprint(f\"Brute-Force Path O(T*L*2^d)  : {np.round(phi_bruteforce, 5).tolist()}\")\nprint(f\"Max |TreeSHAP - BruteForce|  : {np.max(np.abs(phi_treeshap - phi_bruteforce)):.2e}\")\nprint(f\"Efficiency Check (Base+Sum)  : {base_val + np.sum(phi_treeshap):.6f} vs Pred={pred_rf:.6f}\")\nprint(\"Perbandingan Pertumbuhan Operasi untuk T=100, L=64, D=6:\")\nfor dim in [5, 15, 30, 60]:\n    ops_tree = 100 * 64 * (6 ** 2)\n    ops_exp = 100 * 64 * (2 ** dim)\n    print(f\"  d={dim:2d} | TreeSHAP ~ {ops_tree:>10,d} ops | Brute-Force ~ {ops_exp:.2e} ops\")",
          "expectedOutput": "RandomForest (T=12, D=4, d=5) | Base=-0.3332 | Pred=5.3774\nTreeSHAP Polinomial O(TLD^2) : [3.08883, 0.73306, 1.67682, 0.21188, 0.0]\nBrute-Force Path O(T*L*2^d)  : [3.08883, 0.73306, 1.67682, 0.21188, 0.0]\nMax |TreeSHAP - BruteForce|  : 2.22e-16\nEfficiency Check (Base+Sum)  : 5.377383 vs Pred=5.377383\nPerbandingan Pertumbuhan Operasi untuk T=100, L=64, D=6:\n  d= 5 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 2.05e+05 ops\n  d=15 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 2.10e+08 ops\n  d=30 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 6.87e+12 ops\n  d=60 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 7.38e+21 ops",
          "actualOutput": "RandomForest (T=12, D=4, d=5) | Base=-0.3332 | Pred=5.3774\nTreeSHAP Polinomial O(TLD^2) : [3.08883, 0.73306, 1.67682, 0.21188, 0.0]\nBrute-Force Path O(T*L*2^d)  : [3.08883, 0.73306, 1.67682, 0.21188, 0.0]\nMax |TreeSHAP - BruteForce|  : 2.22e-16\nEfficiency Check (Base+Sum)  : 5.377383 vs Pred=5.377383\nPerbandingan Pertumbuhan Operasi untuk T=100, L=64, D=6:\n  d= 5 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 2.05e+05 ops\n  d=15 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 2.10e+08 ops\n  d=30 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 6.87e+12 ops\n  d=60 | TreeSHAP ~    230,400 ops | Brute-Force ~ 7.38e+21 ops",
          "explanation": "Mengimplementasikan subrutin EXTEND dan UNWIND TreeSHAP (Lundberg) langsung di atas RandomForestRegressor.estimators_[].tree_ dan mencocokkannya dengan brute-force O(2^d) hingga selisih 2.22e-16, sekaligus membandingkan ledakan operasi 230.400 vs 7.38e+21 di d=60.",
