          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef audit_and_equalize_odds(y_true, y_prob, group) -> tuple[float, float, float, float, float]:\n    y_true = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n    y_prob = np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float)\n    group = np.asarray(group, dtype=int)\n    def metrics(pred):\n        m0, m1 = (group == 0), (group == 1)\n        dir_r = float(np.mean(pred[m1]) / max(np.mean(pred[m0]), 1e-9))\n        tpr0 = float(np.mean(pred[m0 & (y_true == 1)]))\n        tpr1 = float(np.mean(pred[m1 & (y_true == 1)]))\n        fpr0 = float(np.mean(pred[m0 & (y_true == 0)]))\n        fpr1 = float(np.mean(pred[m1 & (y_true == 0)]))\n        return dir_r, max(abs(tpr0 - tpr1), abs(fpr0 - fpr1)), float(np.mean(pred == y_true)), min(tpr0, tpr1)\n    dir_base, eod_base, _, _ = metrics((y_prob >= 0.50).astype(int))\n    grid = np.linspace(0.20, 0.80, 61)\n    best = (1e9, -1.0, 0.50, 0.50)\n    for t0 in grid:\n        for t1 in grid:\n            pred = np.where(group == 0, y_prob >= t0, y_prob >= t1).astype(int)\n            _, eod, acc, min_tpr = metrics(pred)\n            if min_tpr >= 0.50:\n                if (eod < best[0] - 1e-9) or (abs(eod - best[0]) <= 1e-9 and acc > best[1]):\n                    best = (eod, acc, float(t0), float(t1))\n    return (round(dir_base, 4), round(eod_base, 4), round(best[0], 4), round(best[2], 2), round(best[3], 2))\n```"
